@title  PCSE00093 - boot -> first-run profile -> practice arena -> KICK-OFF exhibition -> a live match
@game   PCSE00093
@shot-every 300

# WHAT THIS RECIPE IS FOR
# ----------------------
# Rendering, audio and frame-rate coverage of FIFA Soccer 13 GAMEPLAY: the practice arena, the
# front-end menus over their 3D arena background, a stadium load, the pre-match walk-out and
# line-up cinematics and then a live exhibition match (Chicago Fire v Columbus Crew, the
# first-run defaults) played with the face buttons and the left stick.
#
# WHAT A RUN OF THIS LOOKS LIKE (2026-10-05, native headless, one baton - session frames):
#   f000000-f002900  legal screens, licence wall, EA SPORTS intro movie
#   f003030          title "Press START button"; START -> the autosave notice (game-drawn)
#   f003520          CROSS answers it; profile setup (skill / controls / favourite team), five
#                    touch-control tip pages and a tips dialog, all advanced with CROSS
#   f006100-f006640  the practice ARENA loads; the player can run and shoot
#   f006720          START -> main menu (KICK-OFF > EXHIBITION MATCH is the default item)
#   f007130-f011140  controller select, home team, away team, both kits, pre-match: all CROSS
#   f011380          the stadium loads; "PRESS START BUTTON TO PLAY"
#   f013550          START -> broadcast intro, walk-out, line-ups, formations
#   f017600          KICK-OFF; live play from here (0:11 on the clock at f17800)
#
# HOW IT IS TIMED - BY WHAT THE GUEST CALLS, NOT BY FRAME
# The frames above are one engine's. Under the multi-threaded engine the same frame-timed
# presses missed the title screen entirely (the intro and loads take a different number of
# frames), so every transition here is a `@wait call` on a host call the title makes exactly
# when the next screen is up, found from a host-call listing of a native run
# (VITASLOP_NID_DIGEST):
#   sceAppUtilSaveDataSlotGetParam   the autosave notice was answered (save slots probed)
#   sceNetCtlInetGetInfo             once, after the tips dialog - the first-run flow is over
#   sceGxmPrecomputedDrawInit        the arena's models are built (f6637), then AGAIN when the
#                                    main menu opens its background (f6782) - two holds
#   sceGxmDrawInstanced              first drawn by the stadium (f11379), and next only after
#                                    START on "PRESS START BUTTON TO PLAY" (f13555)
# Each hold PULSES the button its screens advance with, so a screen that is already up, or one
# that opens late, is answered either way. Every screen between two anchors takes that same
# button: CROSS is "advance"/"select default" on every profile, tips and menu page, and START
# would pause a match - which is why START is only ever pulsed into a hold that a START ends.
#
# CONTROLS (Classic, the first-run default): left stick move, R sprint, CROSS short pass,
# CIRCLE shoot, SQUARE lob, TRIANGLE through ball.
0: @section boot
# The title takes START and ignores CROSS; the autosave notice behind it takes CROSS and ignores
# START; and the calls around the intro movie that could split the two differ between engines
# (the movie's file closes ~f2660 natively and before f1500 in the browser). So ONE hold pulses
# BOTH buttons from the legal screens on: START also skips the movie, and whichever screen is
# up takes its own button. It releases when the answered notice probes the save slots.
1000: @wait call sceAppUtilSaveDataSlotGetParam pulse start+cross 60

3100: @section first-run-profile-and-tips
3100: @wait call sceNetCtlInetGetInfo pulse cross 60   # 3 profile pages, 5 tip pages, a dialog

# The arena builds its models (a burst of sceGxmPrecomputedDrawInit), and START in the arena opens
# the main menu, which builds ITS background the same way. Two holds on the one call, both
# pulsing START: a START during the arena's load is ignored, so the first is released by the
# arena's own build and the second only by the menu's. (A bare hold on the arena's audio coming
# up, sceNgsVoiceKill, never released under the multi-threaded engine, whose arena loads in a
# different order.)
3200: @section practice-arena
3200: @wait call sceGxmPrecomputedDrawInit pulse start 120
3420: lx=255
3480: ly=0
3540:

3600: @section main-menu
3600: @wait call sceGxmPrecomputedDrawInit pulse start 120   # START opens the main menu

# KICK-OFF > EXHIBITION MATCH, controller select, home team, away team, home kit, away kit and
# the pre-match PLAY MATCH are all the default item, so CROSS walks the whole chain.
3700: @section exhibition-setup
3700: @wait call sceGxmDrawInstanced pulse cross 90   # the stadium starts drawing

3900: @section press-start
3900: @wait call sceGxmDrawInstanced pulse start 120   # "PRESS START BUTTON TO PLAY"

# The broadcast intro runs ~4000 frames (walk-out, line-ups, both formations); CROSS skips a
# shot of it where it can, and in play it is a short pass - so the match loop below is safe to
# start straight away.
4000: @section intro-and-match
4100: lx=255 r
4190: cross
4202: lx=200 ly=40
4290: circle
4302: lx=60 ly=128
4380: triangle
4392: lx=255 ly=200 r
4470: square
